cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use membw in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "membw: achieved memory bandwidth with a provenance record"
abstract: >-
  membw measures the achieved memory bandwidth ceiling of a machine and
  reports it against the theoretical peak derived from the readable memory
  configuration. Each run carries a provenance record naming the code path,
  the CPU affinity mask actually in effect, the frequency governor, the
  working set relative to the last-level cache, and every source that could
  not be read. membw reports per CPU cluster as well as in aggregate, and
  refuses to present a figure taken under conditions that invalidate it.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/membw"
url: "https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/membw"
keywords:
